# D[cell-area]: the geometric area of the first two cell vectors, on
# changing rectangular and tilted cells, in double and mixed precision.
# The oracle is the cross product of the checkpoint vectors, including
# b_x != 0; fixed-height coupling also checks A = V / Lz at every output.
# REQUIRES: hdf5
# RUN: rm -rf %t
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check_area.py %S %t cpu mdir | FileCheck %s
# CHECK: cell area, units, log agreement, and exact continuation: ok
